---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/ui/Faq.astro';
import Related from '../../components/ui/Related.astro';
const steps = [['Create your Paystack account', 'Sign up at paystack.com with your business email.'], ['Verify your business', 'Upload your registration documents and bank details so you can accept live payments.'], ['Get your API keys', 'Copy your test keys first. Live keys come after verification.'], ['Add checkout to your site', 'Use Paystack Popup or a payment link on your product and booking buttons.'], ['Test, then go live', 'Run a few test payments, check the receipt emails, then swap in your live keys.']];
const title = 'How to take Paystack payments on your website in Nigeria';
const ld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, datePublished: '2026-11-01', dateModified: '2026-11-01', author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Oladele Ibraheem' }, publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Wintech Studio' } }, { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'HowTo', name: title, step: steps.map(([n, t], i) => ({ '@type': 'HowToStep', position: i + 1, name: n, text: t })) }];
---
<Page title={`${title} · Wintech Studio`} description="Open a Paystack account, verify your business, add checkout to your site and test before going live. Card, bank transfer and USSD." crumbs={[['Guides', '/guides'], ['Payments', '/guides/paystack-payments-on-your-website']]} jsonld={ld}>
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap art">
      <article>
        <p class="mono k">Guide · Payments</p>
        <h1 class="h1">{title}</h1>
        <p class="meta">Updated 1 Nov 2026 · 6 min read · By Oladele Ibraheem</p>
        <div class="short" id="short"><p class="mono">Short answer</p><p>Open a Paystack account, verify your business, then add Paystack checkout to your site. Customers can pay by card, bank transfer or USSD, and the money settles to your bank account. Test everything in test mode before you switch to live keys.</p></div>
        <h2 id="need">What you need before you start</h2>
        <p>A registered business (or a starter account for testing), a bank account in the business name, and a website you can edit. If your site is on Wintech Templates or Astro, the checkout is already built in.</p>
        <h2 id="steps">The steps</h2>
        <ol class="steps">{steps.map(([n, t], i) => <li><span>{i + 1}</span><div><h3>{n}</h3><p>{t}</p></div></li>)}</ol>
        <h2 id="mistakes">Common mistakes</h2>
        <p>Leaving test keys on a live site, not showing delivery fees before checkout, and sending customers to a payment page that does not look like your brand.</p>
      </article>
      <aside>
        <nav class="toc"><p class="mono">On this page</p>{[['short', 'Short answer'], ['need', 'What you need'], ['steps', 'The steps'], ['mistakes', 'Common mistakes']].map(([h, t]) => <a href={`#${h}`}>{t}</a>)}</nav>
        <div class="cta"><h3>Want us to set it up for you?</h3><p>We build stores with Paystack checkout, delivery fees by area and receipts that send themselves. Websites and stores from $1,200.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/services/websites#brief">Build your brief</a></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Faq items={[['Do customers need a Paystack account to pay?', 'No. They pay with a card, a bank transfer or USSD on the checkout. Only you need an account.'], ['How long does verification take?', 'It depends on your documents. You can build and test with test keys while you wait.'], ['Can I use Paystack on Instagram or WhatsApp?', 'Yes, with payment links. A website gives you one checkout for every channel.'], ['Do you charge a cut of my sales?', 'No. Paystack charges its own fee per payment. We charge for the build, not your sales.']]} />
  <Related items={[['Compare', 'Custom website or Wintech Templates', '/compare/custom-website-vs-wintech-templates'], ['Industry', 'Websites and AI for salons in Lagos', '/industries/salons'], ['Service', 'Websites and stores', '/services/websites']]} />
</Page>
<style>
  .art{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,760px) 340px;gap:80px;justify-content:space-between}.k{color:var(--sig)}.meta{color:var(--fg-2);font-size:14px}
  article h2{font-size:28px;margin:48px 0 14px;letter-spacing:-.01em;scroll-margin-top:100px}article p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--fg-2)}
  .short{background:var(--soft,#EEF1FF);padding:24px;margin-top:32px;scroll-margin-top:100px}.short p:last-child{color:var(--fg);margin:8px 0 0}:root[data-theme="dark"] .short{background:#161C33}
  .steps{list-style:none;padding:0;display:grid;gap:8px}.steps li{display:flex;gap:16px;border:1px solid var(--rule);background:var(--card);padding:20px}.steps span{flex:none;width:32px;height:32px;background:var(--ink);color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:600;font-size:14px}.steps h3{font-size:17px;margin:4px 0}.steps p{margin:0;font-size:15px}
  aside{position:sticky;top:120px;align-self:start;display:grid;gap:32px}.toc{display:grid;gap:10px}.toc a{color:var(--fg-2);text-decoration:none;border-left:2px solid var(--rule);padding-left:14px}.toc a:hover{color:var(--fg);border-color:var(--sig)}
  .cta{background:#0A0E17;color:#fff;padding:24px;display:grid;gap:10px}.cta p{color:#A1A1AA;font-size:14px;margin:0}.cta h3{margin:0;font-size:20px}
  @media (max-width:1023px){.art{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:40px}aside{position:static}}
</style>
